'' RUN: '@f' and 'procptr( f )' over an overload set take the overload whose signature
'' the TARGET's type names -- a store, an initialiser, an argument, a field. The address
'' was always the first overload's, so 'p( 1.5 )' through a 'sub( byval as double )'
'' ran the LONG body with a double's bits. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/procptr-overload-target.bas -o tests/codegen/procptrovl.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/procptrovl.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: f double 1.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: f double 2.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: f double 3.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: f double 4.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: f double 5.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: f long 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: g string x
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: g long9
